{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg", "text": "Look at a team that is working at optimum performance, and you'll find that every member of that team has a clear role and responsibilities. Despite having clearly defined roles and responsibilities, a team still may fall short, not be working up to its full potential. Why? Dr. Belbin has observed people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles\". Since a team is not at its best when it is unbalanced, it is important to make sure it has members with different styles of behavior, or roles, within the team. Belbin has identified nine different roles team members play that factor into team success. He has categorized these into: Action-Oriented, People-Oriented, and Thought-Oriented.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img06.jpg", "text": "Action-Oriented Roles <ul><li>Shapers are dynamic, often extroverted people. They enjoy being the ones to challenge other team members to improve and excel at identifying the optimum approach to problems. They ensure the team looks at all possibilities. Shapers often view obstacles as interesting problems to be solved, but they can also be argumentative, and may offend others' feelings.</br></br><li>Implementers are practical people, able to take the team's ideas and concepts and work out practical actions and plans to implement them. Generally, they tend to be conservative, efficient, and very well-organized people. You can rely on them to make sure that the job gets done. However, they can often not only be inflexible, but find change difficult and be a little resistant to it.", "time": "43500", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img05.jpg", "text": "<ul><li> Completer-Finishers make sure that things are completed thoroughly. They are detail-oriented and highly aware of the smallest details. As they are concerned with deadlines, they will push the team to ensure things are finished on, or before the time they are needed. They are ready to work harder in case unforeseen issues arise. They may be described as perfectionists who are conscientious and anxious. Delegating is not something they do well.", "time": "93000", "id": 3}]}}], "_data": []}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can discuss reasons and results of an event or action related to work and jobs. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about things, actions, events, or people in a work environment.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about team roles.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think people take on different roles in a team? What kind of roles are they?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Why is it important to have different roles in a team?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's assess the team!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"con