ialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fall short", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fail to attain a specified amount, level, or degree", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We will fall short of our expectations. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about teams.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "full potential", "type": "name"}, {"content": "succeed as well as you possibly can", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Despite having clear roles and responsibilities, a team will fall short of its full potential. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "team role", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the position that someone has in a group of people who have been chosen to work together to do a particular job", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Dr. Belbin has observed people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles.\"", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unbalanced", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not equal because one person has more influence, power etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Since a team is not at its best when it is unbalanced, it is important to make sure it has members with different styles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to categorize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put \u200bpeople or things into \u200bgroups with the same \u200bfeatures", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He has categorized those roles into three groups.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "argumentative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who often argues with others or enjoys arguing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They can be argumentative, and may offend others' feelings. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inflexible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwilling to make even the slightest change in one's attitudes, plans etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: However, they may be inflexible and can be somewhat resistant to change. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "detail oriented", "type": "name"}, {"content": "spending a lot of time, effort, or attention to details", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are detail-oriented and pay close attention to small details. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reason Clauses: <span class=\"italic\">Since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">As</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Just in case</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are different linking words you can use to introduce reason clauses. Using this type of structure helps to make your writing and speaking sound more professional.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Since and As </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">since</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as </span></span>to introduce reasons that the listener or reader already knows.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Since </span>you're new here, I can show you around the office.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As </span>you've already been introduced to everyone, we can begin the meeting.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">(Just) in case </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">just in case</span> </span>to talk about things that may possibly happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'll send you the outline again <span class=\"strong\">just in case</span> you forget it at home.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Since a team is not at its best when it is unbalanced, it is important to make sure it has members with different styles of behavior, or roles, within the team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As they are concerned with deadlines, they will push the team to ensure things are finished on, or before, the time they are needed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are ready to work harder in case unforeseen issues arise. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Simple Present, Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "It is important not to confuse the name of a verb tense with the way you use it to talk about time. <br/>  A <span class=\"strong\">Present tense</span> does not always refer to present time - it can refer to the future or the past. <br/> Let's review and compare the present tenses.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">need </span>a coffee.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">arrives </span>tomorrow.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m having </span>lunch with friends right now.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m meeting </span>her tomorrow for coffee.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Perfect</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have seen </span>the movie Titanic.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have completed </span>all my work.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "When a team <span class=\"strong\">is performing </span>at its best, you'll usually find that each team member has a clear role and clear responsibilities. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Dr. Belbin <span class=\"strong\">has observed</span> people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles.\" ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Since teams <span class=\"strong\">can become</span> unbalanced, it is important to have team members with different styles of behavior or team roles. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Belbin <span class=\"strong\">has identified</span> nine team roles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They <span class=\"strong\">play </span>a factor in team success. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Work in pairs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a PowerPoint or Prezi presentation about action-oriented roles.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make the presentation 2-4 minutes in length.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain each role: shaper, implementer, completer-finisher.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain the personalities of the people in those roles and give some examples.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain the contributions and allowable weaknesses of each role.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I collaborate with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a PowerPoint presentation that is interesting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain action-oriented roles clearly and concisely.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the different types of personalities in the particular roles.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the contributions and allowable weaknesses of each role.", "type": "text"}]}]}